# Benchmark suite report artifacts, for every layer.
#
# Each layer (l1-compressor, l2-module, l3-scenario, l4-end-to-end) also carries
# its own .gitignore. The L1-L3 layers are standalone Cargo workspaces that must
# stay self-contained; L4 is not a Cargo workspace but follows the same
# per-layer-ignore convention. This file is the suite-wide backstop so a new layer
# cannot leak reports before someone remembers to add its ignore rules, and so
# the policy lives in one reviewable place.
#
# Reports are run- and machine-specific: they carry timestamps, host paths,
# server addresses and provenance of whichever checkout happened to be on the
# runner. Committing them creates diff noise and, more importantly, is how
# environment details end up in a public repository. Generate them locally or in
# CI and attach them to the PR instead.
**/reports/
**/*_REPORT.md
**/*_REPORT_zh.md
**/*_REPORT_DIFF.md
**/report.json

# Probe caches hold model responses keyed by prompt, which means payload
# contents; they are rebuildable and stay local.
**/.probe_cache.json

# Build output of the per-layer workspaces.
**/target/

# Python bytecode from the scenario generators and workers.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
